  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nThe expression: 10 + 3{(3)/(5)} div [ 2{(2)/(3)} div left{ 7{(1)/(6)} - ( 2{(1)/(2)} + {(2)/(3)} ) right} ] \n\n**Calculation:**\n\n**Step 1: Solve the innermost bracket**\n\n⇒ 2(1/2) + 2/3 = 5/2 + 2/3\n\nConvert to a common denominator:\n\n⇒ 5/2 = 15/6 and 2/3 = 4/6\n\n⇒ 15/6 + 4/6 = 19/6\n\n**Step 2: Subtract from 7(1/6)**\n\n⇒ 7(1/6) = 43/6\n\n⇒ 43/6 - 19/6 = 24/6 = 4\n\n**Step 3: Divide 2(2/3) by 4**\n\n⇒ 2(2/3) = 8/3\n\n⇒ 8/3 ÷ 4 = 8/3 × 1/4 = 8/12 = 2/3\n\n**Step 4: Divide 3(3/5) by 2/3**\n\n⇒ 3(3/5) = 18/5\n\n⇒ 18/5 ÷ 2/3 = 18/5 × 3/2 = 54/10 = 27/5\n\n**Step 5: Add 10 to the result**\n\n⇒ 10 + 27/5 = 50/5 + 27/5 = 77/5\n\n**∴ The value of the expression is 77/5.**",
